# (build 100b, 100c) The Escape menu's COMPUTER PLAYS and SPEED. On the
# title, Escape; down six stops (four before build 105's CRT, five before
# build 110's AUDIO) is COMPUTER PLAYS: its lamp, then where it
# starts (NEW GAME: the route has no slots of its own, and left/right find
# none to step to). C lights the lamp and the menu stays up (100c: closing
# the menu with the lamp lit is what starts the computer, in main.c; with it
# put out, what hands the pad back). Down one more is SPEED, C to FAST and
# back to NORMAL; (build 120) C steps NORMAL, AUTO, 2X, AUTO 2X, FAST and
# round to NORMAL, a shot of each (16 ticks apart, the lamp's lit half).
# Up, C to put the lamp out, B to close. The probe has no
# main.c: nothing starts here. The route reads its own settings.json, never
# the player's. The waits put the cursor's lamp in its lit half.
start new
wait screen title
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press right
expect setting computer off
wait ticks 7
shot menu_computer_plays
press c
expect setting computer on
expect escape-menu open
wait ticks 5
shot menu_computer_lit
press down
press c
expect setting speed auto
wait ticks 10
shot menu_speed_auto
press c
expect setting speed 2x
wait ticks 14
shot menu_speed_2x
press c
expect setting speed auto_2x
wait ticks 14
shot menu_speed_auto_2x
press c
expect setting speed fast
wait ticks 14
shot menu_speed_fast
press c
expect setting speed normal
press up
press c
expect setting computer off
press b
expect escape-menu closed
expect screen title
